A revoke that recurses into each child
takes a frame per level of the derivation tree,
and a deep enough tree overflows the kernel's stack.
It revokes the same nodes, so only the stack check catches it.

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -198,3 +198,5 @@ void cap_revoke(struct cap *n)
 {
-    cap_revoke_below(n);
+    while (n->child != 0) {
+        cap_revoke(node(n->child));
+    }
     detach(n, false);
